.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-RHEL-COMPOSER-BUILD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-rhel-composer-build
.Nd build the lab's RHEL golden on a registered RHEL host with Red Hat's image builder
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Red Hat no longer lets a portal user name and password download its cloud
image through the API.
On a kldload host installed as RHEL and registered with Red Hat,
.Nm
has osbuild-composer assemble one from the host's own entitlement
instead, writes it to the ZFS volume
.Pa rpool/vms/klab-golden-rhel
and snapshots it as
.Ql @golden ,
the sixth distribution beside the lab's other five.
It takes 15 to 25 minutes, in the background.
.Pp
.Pa kldload-rhel-composer.service
runs it at first boot when the installer left
.Pa /var/lib/klab/.rhel-composer-pending
and the lab was asked for.
It does nothing when the golden exists, and stops early, saying why, when
the host is not registered, composer is not installed, or a volume of that
name is left from a run that did not finish.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/lib/klab/.rhel-composer-pending
Present until the golden is built.
.It Pa /usr/local/share/kldload/rhel-cloud.toml
The blueprint.
.It Pa /var/lib/klab/images/
Where the image is downloaded before it is written to the volume.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when built, already built, or not wanted; 1 when it could not build,
logged to the journal as
.Ql kldload-rhel-composer .
.Sh EXAMPLES
Building it by hand after registering; not run for this page:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# subscription-manager register
# systemctl start kldload-rhel-composer
# journalctl -t kldload-rhel-composer -f
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr composer-cli 1 ,
.Xr klab 8 ,
.Xr kvm-clone 8 ,
.Xr subscription-manager 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-19 it ran on every RHEL install, the lab asked for or not, and
failed on a plain desktop.
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: a volume left by an unfinished run made
it fail again only after the whole compose.
